# direnv loads the default devShell on entry, so `nix develop` stops being something to
# remember. It prepends to PATH -- everything you have installed stays reachable.
#
# `extra-`, not `experimental-features`: additive, so it cannot clobber a nix.conf that
# already sets others. Needed because direnv shells out to `nix print-dev-env`.
export NIX_CONFIG="extra-experimental-features = nix-command flakes"

# The default shell only. `.#cross` and `.#deps` stay explicit: wine alone pulls in a
# multimedia and X11 graph larger than every other tool here put together.
use flake
